From ef11513e0d1183a529e82c6321a7533c87e28af4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:02:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-sync): audit abandoned containment-refused
 dependency deletes [daveey]

A refused historical unlink left the canonical link live but local deletion
intent and its tombstone unresolved. The generic resolver correctly refused
that tombstone; retrying after containment release would perform unintended
new lifecycle work. No explicit audit-preserving abandonment API existed.

Add per-link token-bound preview/apply with completed diagnostic refresh,
authenticated empty-head cuts, endpoint/containment identity proof and local
transactional compare-and-set. Apply retains original operation/event bytes in
an immutable hashed receipt and clears only the covered stale tombstone.
Normal sync retires only exact receipt-covered operations while retaining the
canonical dependency and all history. No task, link or lease writes are made.

Proof so far: canonical three-delete RED (missing API), GREEN; sync-under-lock
RED (busy refresh), GREEN; audit identity/clock RED, GREEN; CLI/parser RED,
GREEN. Current focused suite passes. Broader regressions, per-guard mutation
proof, final full check, independent exact-head review and CI still required
before landing. No live repair performed; operational owner retains live proof.

Co-Authored-By: GPT 6.1 Sol <noreply@openai.com>
